WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.167
Welcome. This class teaches a disciplined
way to decide whether

2
00:00:04.167 --> 00:00:08.333
an agent result deserves acceptance. We
will review a synthetic

3
00:00:08.333 --> 00:00:12.500
Orion support dossier, qualify an offline
checker, and then test

4
00:00:12.500 --> 00:00:16.667
our reasoning on an independent Lyra case.
Keep the work

5
00:00:16.667 --> 00:00:20.833
order visible. A fluent completion summary
is only a claim

6
00:00:20.833 --> 00:00:25.000
until artifacts, authority, and observed
state support it.

7
00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:28.833
Start with the work order, not the agent
summary. Give

8
00:00:28.833 --> 00:00:32.667
every acceptance criterion a separate row.
Record the exact artifact

9
00:00:32.667 --> 00:00:36.500
or postcondition required, its evidence
reference and revision, the observation,

10
00:00:36.500 --> 00:00:40.333
your inference, the status, and the next
action. This order

11
00:00:40.333 --> 00:00:44.167
prevents polished language from hiding
omitted requirements or silently changing

12
00:00:44.167 --> 00:00:48.000
the scope.

13
00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:52.200
Now trace material claims. Compare exact
source words, revision, authority,

14
00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:56.400
effective date, scope, and provenance.
Citation presence is not support.

15
00:00:56.400 --> 00:01:00.600
Record what the excerpt directly states
before recording your conclusion.

16
00:01:00.600 --> 00:01:04.800
A checker can compare annotations and
references, but a human

17
00:01:04.800 --> 00:01:09.000
must decide whether natural language
actually supports the claim.

18
00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:13.400
In Orion, the archived policy says 45 days
for qualifying

19
00:01:13.400 --> 00:01:17.800
earlier orders. It is superseded. The
current revision says 30

20
00:01:17.800 --> 00:01:22.200
days for deliveries in the work-order
scope. Therefore the claimed

21
00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:26.600
current 45-day window is unsupported. The
same current excerpt supports

22
00:01:26.600 --> 00:01:31.000
a separate seven-day escalation period
after the first support response.

23
00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:35.200
Next inspect authority independently of
outcome. The approval binds the

24
00:01:35.200 --> 00:01:39.400
synthetic reviewer to a draft operation on
one ticket and

25
00:01:39.400 --> 00:01:43.600
tenant. The trace attempts an external
send. Actor, target, and

26
00:01:43.600 --> 00:01:47.800
tenant match, but operation authorization
fails. Preserve both findings. Correct

27
00:01:47.800 --> 00:01:52.000
binding does not repair an unauthorized
operation.

28
00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:55.833
The send attempt timed out, and the
independent ledger state

29
00:01:55.833 --> 00:01:59.667
is unknown. Timeout proves neither
delivery nor absence. Preserve the

30
00:01:59.667 --> 00:02:03.500
correlation identifier and ask the
authorized system owner to reconcile

31
00:02:03.500 --> 00:02:07.333
it. Do not retry, reverse, or widen access
on your

32
00:02:07.333 --> 00:02:11.167
own. Unknown is a useful status because it
prevents duplicate

33
00:02:11.167 --> 00:02:15.000
or unauthorized effects.

34
00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:18.667
The ticket snapshot records that an
internal draft exists. That

35
00:02:18.667 --> 00:02:22.333
verifies only the draft criterion. It does
not prove external

36
00:02:22.333 --> 00:02:26.000
delivery. The test report validates format
and length only. It

37
00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:29.667
does not validate policy truth,
authorization, account isolation, or a

38
00:02:29.667 --> 00:02:33.333
real external outcome. Match every test
result to its declared

39
00:02:33.333 --> 00:02:37.000
scope.

40
00:02:37.000 --> 00:02:40.800
Build the Orion matrix now. Use five rows.
Mark the

41
00:02:40.800 --> 00:02:44.600
policy row, draft row, authorization row,
external-postcondition row, and

42
00:02:44.600 --> 00:02:48.400
target-binding row. For each row, write
one observation, one inference,

43
00:02:48.400 --> 00:02:52.200
and one next action. Keep the supported
seven-day claim even

44
00:02:52.200 --> 00:02:56.000
though the all-claims criterion fails.

45
00:04:26.000 --> 00:04:30.167
Check your first diagnostic. If you marked
the 45-day claim

46
00:04:30.167 --> 00:04:34.333
verified merely because it had a citation,
the causal error

47
00:04:34.333 --> 00:04:38.500
is that you checked presence rather than
support. If you

48
00:04:38.500 --> 00:04:42.667
marked every policy claim false, you lost
the separately supported

49
00:04:42.667 --> 00:04:46.833
seven-day statement. The correct C1 result
is failed because one

50
00:04:46.833 --> 00:04:51.000
required material claim conflicts with
current scope.

51
00:04:51.000 --> 00:04:55.200
Correct reasoning compares exact words,
revision, freshness, authority, and scope.

52
00:04:55.200 --> 00:04:59.400
Citation counting misses the superseded
limitation. Blanket rejection also loses

53
00:04:59.400 --> 00:05:03.600
a supported claim. Preserve claim-level
findings, then apply the criterion

54
00:05:03.600 --> 00:05:07.800
rule. Because every material claim must be
supported, one unsupported

55
00:05:07.800 --> 00:05:12.000
current-policy claim causes the combined
criterion to fail.

56
00:05:12.000 --> 00:05:15.800
For authority, ask whether matching target
and tenant make the

57
00:05:15.800 --> 00:05:19.600
send authorized. They do not. The
operation differs from the

58
00:05:19.600 --> 00:05:23.400
approved draft operation. C3 is failed,
while C5 remains verified.

59
00:05:23.400 --> 00:05:27.200
Separating those rows shows exactly what
was correct and what

60
00:05:27.200 --> 00:05:31.000
crossed the boundary.

61
00:05:31.000 --> 00:05:35.200
If you verified C3 because the ticket and
tenant matched,

62
00:05:35.200 --> 00:05:39.400
you omitted the operation field. If you
failed C5 because

63
00:05:39.400 --> 00:05:43.600
the operation was unauthorized, you merged
two independent requirements. Exact

64
00:05:43.600 --> 00:05:47.800
review preserves both facts: the trace is
correctly bound to

65
00:05:47.800 --> 00:05:52.000
the requested resource, and the attempted
operation exceeds approval.

66
00:05:52.000 --> 00:05:55.833
Now qualify the offline lab. From the
repository root, change

67
00:05:55.833 --> 00:05:59.667
into the lab directory before running
commands. The exact commands

68
00:05:59.667 --> 00:06:03.500
are displayed rather than read as long
paths. The lab

69
00:06:03.500 --> 00:06:07.333
uses synthetic fixtures, Node built-ins,
no network, no credentials, and

70
00:06:07.333 --> 00:06:11.167
no external effects. Qualification used
Node.js version 24.18.0, and fifteen

71
00:06:11.167 --> 00:06:15.000
tests passed.

72
00:06:15.000 --> 00:06:18.667
Run the draft-state inspection and
baseline validation. The inspection

73
00:06:18.667 --> 00:06:22.333
derives draft present as true and passes.
The baseline validation

74
00:06:22.333 --> 00:06:26.000
reports structural pass, policy pass,
decision escalate, two verified, two

75
00:06:26.000 --> 00:06:29.667
failed, one unknown, and result pass. That
result means the

76
00:06:29.667 --> 00:06:33.333
packet is consistent with fixture rules,
not that production facts

77
00:06:33.333 --> 00:06:37.000
are proven.

78
00:06:37.000 --> 00:06:41.200
The flawed packet is structurally valid
but fails policy validation.

79
00:06:41.200 --> 00:06:45.400
It wrongly verifies C1, wrongly converts
C4 from unknown to

80
00:06:45.400 --> 00:06:49.600
verified, and accepts instead of
escalating. This is a causal

81
00:06:49.600 --> 00:06:53.800
diagnostic: complete references and valid
JSON cannot repair incorrect evidence

82
00:06:53.800 --> 00:06:58.000
interpretation or a decision that ignores
consequential uncertainty.

83
00:06:58.000 --> 00:07:01.667
If you accepted because structure passed,
you confused shape with

84
00:07:01.667 --> 00:07:05.333
policy consistency. If you verified C4
after the timeout, you

85
00:07:05.333 --> 00:07:09.000
converted missing evidence into an absence
claim. If you accepted

86
00:07:09.000 --> 00:07:12.667
C1 because references were present, you
skipped semantic review. Each

87
00:07:12.667 --> 00:07:16.333
error has a different cause, so each needs
a different

88
00:07:16.333 --> 00:07:20.000
correction.

89
00:07:20.000 --> 00:07:23.667
Try the altered-observation probe. In an
isolated copy, change the

90
00:07:23.667 --> 00:07:27.333
applicable observed Boolean from true to
false. The inspect command

91
00:07:27.333 --> 00:07:31.000
must print false, then fail, and exit with
status one.

92
00:07:31.000 --> 00:07:34.667
Also confirm that empty evidence-reference
arrays are rejected. These probes

93
00:07:34.667 --> 00:07:38.333
show evidence derivation and structural
enforcement rather than stored-output

94
00:07:38.333 --> 00:07:42.000
replay.

95
00:07:42.000 --> 00:07:46.500
Before opening the Lyra solution, review
the changed dossier independently.

96
00:07:46.500 --> 00:07:51.000
Its policy, authorization, operation,
target, tenant, trace, and state are

97
00:07:51.000 --> 00:07:55.500
new inputs. Decide each criterion from
those inputs. Do not

98
00:07:55.500 --> 00:08:00.000
copy Orion's escalation merely because the
matrix shape is similar.

99
00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:33.667
In Lyra, the current excerpt supports both
material claims. Authorization

100
00:09:33.667 --> 00:09:37.333
and trace match on identity, operation,
target, and tenant. Independent

101
00:09:37.333 --> 00:09:41.000
state records the internal note as
present. All five criteria

102
00:09:41.000 --> 00:09:44.667
are verified, so accept is correct within
the synthetic fixture

103
00:09:44.667 --> 00:09:48.333
scope. Success from the trace alone would
not have been

104
00:09:48.333 --> 00:09:52.000
enough.

105
00:09:52.000 --> 00:09:56.000
If you copied Orion's escalation, name the
Lyra row that

106
00:09:56.000 --> 00:10:00.000
remains failed or unknown. There is none
in the supplied

107
00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:04.000
fixture. If you accepted only because the
trace reports success,

108
00:10:04.000 --> 00:10:08.000
your conclusion used insufficient
evidence. Source support, authorization,

109
00:10:08.000 --> 00:10:12.000
binding, and independent state must each
be reviewed.

110
00:10:12.000 --> 00:10:16.000
Correct Lyra reasoning is input-sensitive.
It does not inherit Orion's

111
00:10:16.000 --> 00:10:20.000
result. The current source supports both
claims, the grant and

112
00:10:20.000 --> 00:10:24.000
trace match, and observed state confirms
the internal note. If

113
00:10:24.000 --> 00:10:28.000
any one of those inputs changed, the
affected status and

114
00:10:28.000 --> 00:10:32.000
possibly the decision would change.

115
00:10:32.000 --> 00:10:36.200
Use this decision rule. Accept only when
every mandatory row

116
00:10:36.200 --> 00:10:40.400
has sufficient evidence. Request changes
for a reproducible defect the

117
00:10:40.400 --> 00:10:44.600
author can repair. Escalate when
consequential state is unknown, authority

118
00:10:44.600 --> 00:10:48.800
is missing, or the required decision
exceeds your role. Several

119
00:10:48.800 --> 00:10:53.000
passes never average away one mandatory
failure.

120
00:10:53.000 --> 00:10:56.250
Open the audit activity. Submit the Orion
and Lyra matrices,

121
00:10:56.250 --> 00:10:59.500
reproduced outputs, source observations,
inferences, decisions, and next actions.

122
00:10:59.500 --> 00:11:02.750
Explain what the checker establishes and
what still requires human

123
00:11:02.750 --> 00:11:06.000
judgment.

124
00:14:06.000 --> 00:14:09.800
Before submitting, verify that every
accepted row cites a revision-bound

125
00:14:09.800 --> 00:14:13.600
artifact. Every failed or unknown row must
name the smallest

126
00:14:13.600 --> 00:14:17.400
authorized next action. A draft snapshot
cannot prove delivery. A

127
00:14:17.400 --> 00:14:21.200
format test cannot prove source truth. A
matching target cannot

128
00:14:21.200 --> 00:14:25.000
authorize a different operation.

129
00:14:25.000 --> 00:14:29.000
A strong packet lets another reviewer
reproduce the decision without

130
00:14:29.000 --> 00:14:33.000
trusting the agent summary. It preserves
exact revisions, direct observations,

131
00:14:33.000 --> 00:14:37.000
bounded inferences, failed controls,
unresolved state, and responsible next

132
00:14:37.000 --> 00:14:41.000
actions. It never implies that checker
success establishes semantic truth,

133
00:14:41.000 --> 00:14:45.000
live authorization, or a production
postcondition.

134
00:14:45.000 --> 00:14:48.800
Begin the knowledge check when you can
explain why source

135
00:14:48.800 --> 00:14:52.600
presence is not source support, why draft
state is not

136
00:14:52.600 --> 00:14:56.400
delivery state, why matching target does
not authorize a different

137
00:14:56.400 --> 00:15:00.200
operation, and why timeout remains
unknown. The five assessment questions

138
00:15:00.200 --> 00:15:04.000
use those exact distinctions.

139
00:15:04.000 --> 00:15:07.750
Review begins with requirements and ends
with a decision another

140
00:15:07.750 --> 00:15:11.500
reviewer can reproduce. Preserve
observations, inferences, defects,

141
00:15:11.500 --> 00:15:15.250
unknowns, revisions, and authority
boundaries. The lab is qualified evidence

142
00:15:15.250 --> 00:15:19.000
for its fixture behavior, not production
truth.
